{"id":"mahabharata-2-047","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":47,"title":"सप्तचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 47 · The tribute of the kings","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana lists the wonderful gifts the kings brought Yudhishthira: blankets, skins, gold, horses, elephants and jewels from the mountain peoples, the north and the eastern kings, who were made to wait at the door for want of room.","kn":"ಗಿರಿಜನರು, ಉತ್ತರದವರು, ಪೂರ್ವದ ರಾಜರು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ತಂದ ಕಂಬಳಿ, ಚರ್ಮ, ಚಿನ್ನ, ಕುದುರೆ, ಆನೆ, ರತ್ನಗಳಂಥ ಅದ್ಭುತ ಕಾಣಿಕೆಗಳನ್ನು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಪಟ್ಟಿಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸ್ಥಳವಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಅವರು ದ್ವಾರದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾಯಬೇಕಾಯಿತು.","hi":"दुर्योधन उन अद्भुत उपहारों को गिनाता है जो राजाओं ने युधिष्ठिर को दिए: पहाड़ी जातियों, उत्तर के लोगों और पूर्व के राजाओं के कम्बल, खालें, सोना, घोड़े, हाथी और रत्न, जिन्हें स्थान न होने से द्वार पर प्रतीक्षा करनी पड़ी।","te":"గిరిజనులు, ఉత్తరవాసులు, తూర్పు రాజులు యుధిష్ఠిరునికి తెచ్చిన కంబళ్లు, చర్మాలు, బంగారం, గుర్రాలు, ఏనుగులు, రత్నాల వంటి అద్భుత కానుకలను దుర్యోధనుడు ఏకరువు పెడతాడు; చోటు లేక వారు ద్వారం వద్ద వేచి ఉండవలసి వచ్చింది.","ta":"மலைவாழ் இனங்கள், வடநாட்டினர், கிழக்கு மன்னர்கள் யுதிஷ்டிரருக்குக் கொண்டு வந்த கம்பளிகள், தோல்கள், பொன், குதிரைகள், யானைகள், ரத்தினங்கள் போன்ற அற்புதப் பரிசுகளைத் துரியோதனன் பட்டியலிடுகிறான்; இடமின்றி அவர்கள் வாயிலில் காத்திருக்க வேண்டியதாயிற்று.","ml":"രാജാക്കന്മാർ യുധിഷ്ഠിരന് കൊണ്ടുവന്ന അദ്ഭുത സമ്മാനങ്ങൾ ദുര്യോധനൻ പട്ടികപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു: പുതപ്പുകൾ, തോലുകൾ, സ്വർണം, കുതിരകൾ, ആനകൾ, പർവതവർഗക്കാരുടെ രത്നങ്ങൾ, വടക്കും കിഴക്കുമുള്ള രാജാക്കന്മാരുടെ കാഴ്ചകൾ; സ്ഥലമില്ലാത്തതിനാൽ അവരെ വാതിൽക്കൽ കാത്തുനിർത്തേണ്ടിവന്നുവെന്നും."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.47; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यन्मया पाण्डवानां तु दृष्टं तच्छृणु भारत ।\nआहृतं भूमिपालैर्हि वसु मुख्यं ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, Bharata, what I saw among the Pandavas: the best wealth brought by the kings from here and there."}},{"n":2,"text":"न विन्दे दृढमात्मानं दृष्ट्वाहं तदरेर्धनम् ।\nफलतो भूमितो वापि प्रतिपद्यस्व भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot keep myself steady on seeing that enemy's wealth; take it in, Bharata, whether from fruit or land."}},{"n":3,"text":"ऐडांश्चैलान्वार्षदंशाञ्जातरूपपरिष्कृतान् ।\nप्रावाराजिनमुख्यांश्च काम्बोजः प्रददौ वसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kamboja gave wealth: woollens and silks of the Aida and Varshadamsha kinds, adorned with gold, and fine cloaks and hides."}},{"n":4,"text":"अश्वांस्तित्तिरिकल्माषांस्त्रिशतं शुकनासिकान् ।\nउष्ट्रवामीस्त्रिशतं च पुष्टाः पीलुशमीङ्गुदैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He gave three hundred horses speckled like partridges and with parrot-like noses, and three hundred she-camels fattened on pilu, shami and ingudi."}},{"n":5,"text":"गोवासना ब्राह्मणाश्च दासमीयाश्च सर्वशः ।\nप्रीत्यर्थं ते महाभागा धर्मराज्ञो महात्मनः ।\nत्रिखर्वं बलिमादाय द्वारि तिष्ठन्ति वारिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins clothed in cow-hide and servants of every kind, great and fortunate, bring tribute of three kharvas for the pleasure of Yudhishthira, the great-souled king of dharma, and stand held back at the door."}},{"n":6,"text":"कमण्डलूनुपादाय जातरूपमयाञ्शुभान् ।\nएवं बलिं प्रदायाथ प्रवेशं लेभिरे ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking fine golden water-pots, they gave tribute thus and then gained admission."}},{"n":7,"text":"शतं दासीसहस्राणां कार्पासिकनिवासिनाम् ।\nश्यामास्तन्व्यो दीर्घकेश्यो हेमाभरणभूषिताः ।\nशूद्रा विप्रोत्तमार्हाणि राङ्कवान्यजिनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred thousand maidservants living among cotton workers, dark, slender, long-haired, adorned with gold, and Shudras brought hides and ranku deerskins fit for the best brahmins."}},{"n":8,"text":"बलिं च कृत्स्नमादाय भरुकच्छनिवासिनः ।\nउपनिन्युर्महाराज हयान्गान्धारदेशजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the people living at Bharukachchha brought all their tribute, great king, and horses born in the land of Gandhara."}},{"n":9,"text":"इन्द्रकृष्टैर्वर्तयन्ति धान्यैर्नदीमुखैश्च ये ।\nसमुद्रनिष्कुटे जाताः परिसिन्धु च मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who live on grain watered by Indra's rain or by river mouths, and people born on the sea coast and around the Sindhu,"}},{"n":10,"text":"ते वैरामाः पारदाश्च वङ्गाश्च कितवैः सह ।\nविविधं बलिमादाय रत्नानि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Vairamas, Paradas, Vangas and Kitavas, with tribute of many kinds and varied jewels,"}},{"n":11,"text":"अजाविकं गोहिरण्यं खरोष्ट्रं फलजं मधु ।\nकम्बलान्विविधांश्चैव द्वारि तिष्ठन्ति वारिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"goats and sheep, cattle and gold, mules and camels, fruit-honey and many sorts of blankets, stand held back at the door."}},{"n":12,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषाधिपः शूरो म्लेच्छानामधिपो बली ।\nयवनैः सहितो राजा भगदत्तो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brave king of Pragjyotisha, Bhagadatta, mighty lord of the Mlecchas, great chariot-warrior, together with the Yavanas,"}},{"n":13,"text":"आजानेयान्हयाञ्शीघ्रानादायानिलरंहसः ।\nबलिं च कृत्स्नमादाय द्वारि तिष्ठति वारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"bringing swift thoroughbred horses fast as the wind and all his tribute, stands at the door held back."}},{"n":14,"text":"अश्मसारमयं भाण्डं शुद्धदन्तत्सरूनसीन् ।\nप्राग्ज्योतिषोऽथ तद्दत्त्वा भगदत्तोऽव्रजत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given vessels made of hard stone, and swords with pure ivory hilts, Bhagadatta of Pragjyotisha then went away."}},{"n":15,"text":"द्व्यक्षांस्त्र्यक्षाँल्ललाटाक्षान्नानादिग्भ्यः समागतान् ।\nऔष्णीषाननिवासांश्च बाहुकान्पुरुषादकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men with two eyes, three eyes, or an eye in the forehead, come from many directions, turbaned or without clothes, Bahukas and man-eaters,"}},{"n":16,"text":"एकपादांश्च तत्राहमपश्यं द्वारि वारितान् ।\nबल्यर्थं ददतस्तस्मै हिरण्यं रजतं बहु ॥","meaning":{"en":"and one-footed men, I saw held back at the door there, offering plenty of gold and silver as tribute."}},{"n":17,"text":"इन्द्रगोपकवर्णाभाञ्शुकवर्णान्मनोजवान् ।\nतथैवेन्द्रायुधनिभान्संध्याभ्रसदृशानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking forest horses swift as thought, coloured like the indragopa insect, like parrots, like Indra's bow, or like evening clouds,"}},{"n":18,"text":"अनेकवर्णानारण्यान्गृहीत्वाश्वान्मनोजवान् ।\nजातरूपमनर्घ्यं च ददुस्तस्यैकपादकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the one-footed men gave him priceless gold."}},{"n":19,"text":"चीनान्हूणाञ्शकानोड्रान्पर्वतान्तरवासिनः ।\nवार्ष्णेयान्हारहूणांश्च कृष्णान्हैमवतांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Chinas, Hunas, Shakas, Odras, mountain-dwellers, the Varshneyas, Harahunas, dark Himalayan people,"}},{"n":20,"text":"न पारयाम्यभिगतान्विविधान्द्वारि वारितान् ।\nबल्यर्थं ददतस्तस्य नानारूपाननेकशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot list all those who came, held back at the door, giving him of many kinds and forms as tribute."}},{"n":21,"text":"कृष्णग्रीवान्महाकायान्रासभाञ्शतपातिनः ।\nआहार्षुर्दशसाहस्रान्विनीतान्दिक्षु विश्रुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They brought ten thousand trained donkeys with dark necks, huge bodied and swift, renowned in all directions."}},{"n":22,"text":"प्रमाणरागस्पर्शाढ्यं बाह्लीचीनसमुद्भवम् ।\nऔर्णं च राङ्कवं चैव कीटजं पट्टजं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wool of Bahlika and China, rich in size, colour and touch, and wool of ranku deer, and cloth of insects and silk,"}},{"n":23,"text":"कुट्टीकृतं तथैवान्यत्कमलाभं सहस्रशः ।\nश्लक्ष्णं वस्त्रमकार्पासमाविकं मृदु चाजिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and other cloth patterned in thousands, lotus-coloured, fine, not cotton, sheep's wool and soft hides."}},{"n":24,"text":"निशितांश्चैव दीर्घासीनृष्टिशक्तिपरश्वधान् ।\nअपरान्तसमुद्भूतांस्तथैव परशूञ्शितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They brought sharp long swords, spears, lances and axes, and keen axes made in the western lands."}},{"n":25,"text":"रसान्गन्धांश्च विविधान्रत्नानि च सहस्रशः ।\nबलिं च कृत्स्नमादाय द्वारि तिष्ठन्ति वारिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Flavours, scents of many kinds, and jewels in thousands: bringing all this tribute, they stand held back at the door."}},{"n":26,"text":"शकास्तुखाराः कङ्काश्च रोमशाः शृङ्गिणो नराः ।\nमहागमान्दूरगमान्गणितानर्बुदं हयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakas, Tukharas, Kankas, hairy men and horned men brought a counted arbuda of horses that go far and wide."}},{"n":27,"text":"कोटिशश्चैव बहुशः सुवर्णं पद्मसंमितम् ।\nबलिमादाय विविधं द्वारि तिष्ठन्ति वारिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And gold in crores and many padmas: bringing many kinds of tribute, they stand held back at the door."}},{"n":28,"text":"आसनानि महार्हाणि यानानि शयनानि च ।\nमणिकाञ्चनचित्राणि गजदन्तमयानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Costly seats, vehicles and beds, decorated with jewels and gold and made of ivory,"}},{"n":29,"text":"रथांश्च विविधाकाराञ्जातरूपपरिष्कृतान् ।\nहयैर्विनीतैः संपन्नान्वैयाघ्रपरिवारणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"chariots of many shapes adorned with gold, fitted with trained horses and covered with tiger skins,"}},{"n":30,"text":"विचित्रांश्च परिस्तोमान्रत्नानि च सहस्रशः ।\nनाराचानर्धनाराचाञ्शस्त्राणि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"varied coverings and jewels in thousands, naracha and half-naracha arrows and weapons of many kinds."}},{"n":31,"text":"एतद्दत्त्वा महद्द्रव्यं पूर्वदेशाधिपो नृपः ।\nप्रविष्टो यज्ञसदनं पाण्डवस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given this great wealth, the king of the eastern country entered the sacrificial hall of the great-souled Pandava."}}]}]}